# Translation Glossary Template — Vietnamese Scholarly Texts

Use this structure when building glossaries for Vietnamese→English translation of historical texts.

## Format

```markdown
# [Source Title] — Translation Glossary (Chapter/Section)

## Proper Names (NEVER translate — keep in Vietnamese)
- [Name] — [role/context], [dates if known]
- ...

## Titles & Terms (translate with explanation on first use, then use English)
- [Vietnamese term] — [English translation] ([context/notes])
- ...

## Treaties & Events
- [Vietnamese name] = [English equivalent / standard Western name]
- ...

## Period Terms
- [term] — [translation / explanation]
- ...
```

## Rules

1. **Proper names section**: Every person, place, dynasty, organization stays in Vietnamese. The glossary entry provides context (who they were, when they lived) so the translator sub-agent can render them accurately in context.

2. **Titles section**: On first occurrence in translation, render as "English (Vietnamese)" — e.g. "French Resident (Khâm sứ)". After first use, English only. The glossary defines the mapping.

3. **Treaties section**: Vietnamese treaties often have both a Vietnamese name and a Western name (e.g. "Hòa ước Quý Mùi" = "Harmand Treaty"). Note both.

4. **Period terms**: Words like "cần vương", "thực dân", "bảo hộ" carry ideological weight. Define them precisely — the translation must preserve the author's political register.

## What to extract from each chapter

Scan the cleaned OCR text for:
- Personal names (including birth names, reign titles, posthumous names)
- Place names (especially historical ones that differ from modern)
- Official titles and ranks (military, civilian, religious)
- Treaty names and dates
- Organizations and movements
- Culturally loaded terms (đồng bào, cần vương, mặt trận, etc.)

## Volume 6 Specific Notes

Volume 6 ("Việt-Nam Cách Mạng Cận Sử") covers ~1885-1910s. Key term clusters:
- Huế court politics: Phụ chính, triều đình, Nam Triều, Hoàng cung, Nội
- French colonial apparatus: Khâm sứ, Tổng Trú sứ, tòa Khâm, bảo hộ, thực dân
- Military: chiến binh, nghĩa quân, pháo thủ, đại đội, trung đội
- Resistance: kháng chiến, bài ngoại, Cần Vương, phong trào
- Treaties: Hòa ước Quý Mùi (1883), Hiệp ước 1884 (Patenôtre)

## Example (from Chapter I sample)

```markdown
## Proper Names (NEVER translate)
- Kiến Phúc (vua) — emperor, reigned 1883-1884
- Nguyễn Văn Tường — regent, power broker at Huế court
- Tôn Thất Thuyết — regent, led resistance after 1885
- Học Phi (Hoàng Thái Phi) — consort of Tự Đức, foster mother of multiple emperors

## Titles & Terms
- vua — emperor (in scholarly context)
- triều đình — court (imperial court at Huế)
- Nam Triều — the Southern Court (Vietnamese imperial government)
- Phụ chính — Regent
- Khâm sứ — French Resident
- tòa Khâm — French Residency
- Hoàng cung — Imperial Palace / Forbidden City
- Nội — Inner Citadel (of Huế)

## Treaties & Events
- Hòa ước Quý Mùi (1883) = Treaty of Huế / Harmand Treaty
- Hiệp ước 1884 = Treaty of 1884 (Patenôtre Treaty)
- thất thủ kinh thành — the fall of the Capital (Huế, 1885)

## Period Terms
- bảo hộ — protectorate
- thực dân — colonialist / colonizer
- kháng chiến — resistance
- Cần Vương — "Aid the King" resistance movement (post-1885)
- mai dốc — malaria (archaic Vietnamese)
```
